1	# Theme Presets
2	
3	Four named, production-ready token stacks. Each is a complete primitive layer for the 3-layer contract in [tokens.md](tokens.md) — map these into your semantic tokens, don't reference them raw from components. Pick one when the project has no token system; if the project has tokens, those win ([SKILL.md](../SKILL.md) Discovery).
4	
5	These are not "styles to sprinkle". A preset is all-or-nothing: mixing Porcelain's radii with Carbon's shadows produces incoherence that reads as generated.
6	
7	**Contrast rule for all presets:** before shipping, verify text pairs with APCA — Lc ≥ 75 for body text, Lc ≥ 60 for large text (≥24px), Lc ≥ 45 for non-text UI. The pairs below are chosen to clear these; re-verify after any tweak.
8	
9	**Default usage:** light mode unless the user asks for dark. Every preset defines both; both must be intentional ([color.md](color.md) dark-mode rules).
10	
11	**Motion tokens:** each preset's `--motion-*` values intentionally override the canonical scale in [motion.md](motion.md) — pace is part of the aesthetic (Signal is fast, Porcelain unhurried). When a preset is active, its values win; the motion.md scale is the default when building without a preset. All values stay within the ≤400ms ceiling.
12	
13	---
14	
15	## Graphite — minimal clean (default)
16	
17	Cool neutrals, one deep accent, hairline borders, tight type. The safe choice for SaaS tools, admin surfaces, and the Command/Overview dashboard compositions. Disappears behind the data — which is the point.
18	
19	```css
20	:root {
21	  /* neutrals — cool, hue 255 */
22	  --gray-0:   oklch(99% 0.002 255);   /* page */
23	  --gray-1:   oklch(97% 0.003 255);   /* raised surface, sidebar tint */
24	  --gray-2:   oklch(93% 0.004 255);   /* hairlines, dividers */
25	  --gray-3:   oklch(86% 0.005 255);   /* disabled fills */
26	  --gray-6:   oklch(55% 0.012 255);   /* secondary text */
27	  --gray-7:   oklch(42% 0.014 255);   /* tertiary headings */
28	  --gray-9:   oklch(18% 0.012 255);   /* primary text */
29	
30	  /* accent — deep indigo */
31	  --accent:        oklch(46% 0.17 275);
32	  --accent-hover:  oklch(41% 0.17 275);
33	  --accent-tint:   oklch(46% 0.17 275 / 0.08);
34	  --on-accent:     oklch(99% 0.002 255);
35	
36	  /* semantic */
37	  --success: oklch(52% 0.13 155);
38	  --warning: oklch(62% 0.14 75);
39	  --danger:  oklch(52% 0.18 25);
40	
41	  /* type — one grotesque sans for everything */
42	  --font-body: var(--font-sans);       /* Inter-class; system-ui acceptable */
43	  --text-body: 14px / 1.5;
44	  --text-display: 28px;                 /* metrics; 36px for hero */
45	  --tracking-display: -0.02em;
46	
47	  /* shape + depth */
48	  --radius-input: 0.375rem;  --radius-card: 0.625rem;  --radius-modal: 0.875rem;
49	  --shadow-card: 0 0 0 1px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.04), 0 1px 2px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.05);
50	  --shadow-overlay: 0 0 0 1px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.05), 0 8px 24px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.12);
51	
52	  /* motion */
53	  --motion-fast: 120ms;  --motion-base: 200ms;  --motion-slow: 320ms;
54	  --ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
55	}
56	```
57	
58	**Dark mapping:** page `oklch(15% 0.012 255)`, raised `oklch(19% 0.012 255)`, hairline `oklch(26% 0.012 255)`, text `oklch(93% 0.004 255)`, accent lifts to `oklch(62% 0.15 275)`, shadows replaced by surface lightness steps.
59	
60	---
61	
62	## Porcelain — soft modern
63	
64	Warm neutrals, terracotta accent, generous radius, soft layered shadows. For products that want approachable over technical: consumer SaaS, onboarding-heavy tools, health/finance for humans. Pairs with VISUAL_DENSITY ≤ 5.
65	
66	```css
67	:root {
68	  --gray-0:   oklch(98.5% 0.004 80);
69	  --gray-1:   oklch(96.5% 0.006 80);
70	  --gray-2:   oklch(92% 0.008 80);
71	  --gray-3:   oklch(85% 0.009 80);
72	  --gray-6:   oklch(54% 0.015 70);
73	  --gray-9:   oklch(22% 0.015 60);
74	
75	  --accent:        oklch(60% 0.13 40);
76	  --accent-hover:  oklch(55% 0.13 40);
77	  --accent-tint:   oklch(60% 0.13 40 / 0.09);
78	  --on-accent:     oklch(98.5% 0.004 80);
79	
80	  --success: oklch(56% 0.12 150);
81	  --warning: oklch(66% 0.13 80);
82	  --danger:  oklch(54% 0.17 28);
83	
84	  /* type — humanist sans body, optional rounded display */
85	  --text-body: 15px / 1.55;
86	  --text-display: 30px;
87	  --tracking-display: -0.015em;
88	
89	  --radius-input: 0.625rem;  --radius-card: 0.875rem;  --radius-modal: 1.25rem;
90	  --shadow-card: 0 1px 2px oklch(30% 0.02 60 / 0.06), 0 4px 12px oklch(30% 0.02 60 / 0.06);
91	  --shadow-overlay: 0 2px 4px oklch(30% 0.02 60 / 0.08), 0 16px 40px oklch(30% 0.02 60 / 0.14);
92	
93	  --motion-fast: 140ms;  --motion-base: 220ms;  --motion-slow: 360ms;
94	  --ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
95	}
96	```
97	
98	**Dark mapping:** keep the warm hue — page `oklch(17% 0.012 70)`, raised `oklch(21% 0.012 70)`; accent lifts to `oklch(70% 0.12 45)`. Warm dark is this preset's signature; switching to cool dark breaks it.
99	
100	---
101	
102	## Carbon — dark premium
103	
104	Dark-first. Deep cool neutrals, elevation by surface tint (not shadow), one restrained luminous accent. For developer tools, monitoring, pro audio/video — products used for hours in the dark. Light mode exists but dark is primary.
105	
106	```css
107	:root {  /* dark IS the root */
108	  --surface-0: oklch(14% 0.012 260);   /* page */
109	  --surface-1: oklch(17.5% 0.012 260); /* card */
110	  --surface-2: oklch(21% 0.012 260);   /* raised: popover, hover */
111	  --surface-3: oklch(25% 0.012 260);   /* highest: modal */
112	  --line:      oklch(28% 0.012 260);   /* hairlines */
113	  --text-1:    oklch(93% 0.005 260);
114	  --text-2:    oklch(70% 0.01 260);
115	  --text-3:    oklch(52% 0.012 260);
116	
117	  --accent:        oklch(78% 0.12 170);  /* luminous mint — reads as light, not paint */
118	  --accent-hover:  oklch(84% 0.12 170);
119	  --accent-tint:   oklch(78% 0.12 170 / 0.10);
120	  --on-accent:     oklch(8% 0.008 260);  /* near-true black — the 14% surface tone fails Lc 60 here */
121	
122	  --success: oklch(74% 0.12 155);
123	  --warning: oklch(78% 0.13 85);
124	  --danger:  oklch(68% 0.16 25);
125	
126	  --text-body: 14px / 1.5;
127	  --text-display: 28px;
128	  --tracking-display: -0.02em;
129	  /* numbers and code in mono; tabular-nums everywhere */
130	
131	  --radius-input: 0.375rem;  --radius-card: 0.625rem;  --radius-modal: 0.875rem;
132	  /* NO drop shadows — elevation = surface step + 1px line. Glow only on the
133	     single primary CTA, subtle: 0 0 16px var(--accent-tint) */
134	
135	  --motion-fast: 120ms;  --motion-base: 180ms;  --motion-slow: 300ms;
136	  --ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
137	}
138	```
139	
140	**Light mapping (secondary):** invert the surface ladder onto Graphite's neutrals; accent darkens to `oklch(50% 0.13 170)`. Don't ship light-Carbon as default — if light is the primary need, pick Graphite.
141	
142	---
143	
144	## Signal — sharp geometric
145	
146	High-contrast, near-mono neutrals, semantic color doing real work, minimal radius, zero decorative depth. For dense data products — the Analytics composition, trading-adjacent surfaces, ops consoles at VISUAL_DENSITY ≥ 8.
147	
148	```css
149	:root {
150	  --gray-0:   oklch(100% 0 0);
151	  --gray-1:   oklch(97% 0 0);
152	  --gray-2:   oklch(91% 0 0);
153	  --gray-6:   oklch(50% 0 0);
154	  --gray-9:   oklch(12% 0 0);
155	
156	  --accent:        oklch(40% 0.16 264);   /* one decisive blue-violet — used ONLY for selection + primary action */
157	  --accent-hover:  oklch(34% 0.16 264);
158	  --accent-tint:   oklch(40% 0.16 264 / 0.08);
159	  --on-accent:     oklch(100% 0 0);
160	
161	  /* semantic carries the information load — held to dots, deltas-on-demand, alerts */
162	  --success: oklch(50% 0.15 150);
163	  --warning: oklch(60% 0.15 70);
164	  --danger:  oklch(50% 0.20 25);
165	
166	  /* type — body sans, ALL numerals mono */
167	  --text-body: 13px / 1.45;
168	  --font-data: var(--font-mono);
169	  --text-display: 26px;
170	  --tracking-display: -0.01em;
171	
172	  --radius-input: 0.125rem;  --radius-card: 0.375rem;  --radius-modal: 0.625rem;
173	  --shadow-card: none;                      /* 1px hairline only */
174	  --shadow-overlay: 0 0 0 1px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.08), 0 6px 20px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.10);
175	
176	  --motion-fast: 100ms;  --motion-base: 160ms;  --motion-slow: 240ms;  /* speed IS the aesthetic */
177	  --ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
178	}
179	```
180	
181	**Dark mapping:** pure-neutral dark — page `oklch(13% 0 0)`, card `oklch(16.5% 0 0)`, hairline `oklch(25% 0 0)`; accent lifts to `oklch(70% 0.13 264)`; semantic hues lift ~20% lightness. The mono-numeral rule does not relax in dark.
182	
183	---
184	
185	## Choosing
186	
187	| Signal in the brief | Preset |
188	|---|---|
189	| "clean", "professional", internal tool, no strong brand | **Graphite** |
190	| "friendly", "approachable", consumer-facing, onboarding matters | **Porcelain** |
191	| "developer tool", "pro", users live in it at night | **Carbon** |
192	| "dense", "fast", data is the product, power users | **Signal** |
193	
194	Brand color exists? Replace `--accent` with the brand hue at the preset's lightness/chroma discipline — the preset survives an accent swap; it does not survive a radius or shadow swap.
195	
196	---
197	
198	## Accent rotation (no brand yet)
199	
200	When the brief has no brand color, **rotate one accent family per build** so outputs don't all land on indigo. Declare the choice in the Craft Read ([craft-intent.md](craft-intent.md) §6). Swap only `--accent`, `--accent-hover`, `--accent-tint`, and `--on-accent` on the chosen preset — keep neutrals, radii, and shadows intact.
201	
202	| Family | Light `--accent` (OKLCH) | Best on preset | Avoid pairing with |
203	|---|---|---|---|
204	| **Indigo** | `oklch(46% 0.17 275)` | Graphite, Signal | — (default; rotate away often) |
205	| **Teal** | `oklch(48% 0.12 195)` | Graphite, Carbon | Porcelain terracotta clash |
206	| **Rose** | `oklch(52% 0.14 15)` | Porcelain, Graphite | Signal high-contrast grids |
207	| **Amber** | `oklch(58% 0.14 75)` | Porcelain, Graphite | Carbon mint accent |
208	| **Forest** | `oklch(46% 0.11 155)` | Porcelain, Graphite | Signal blue-violet default |
209	
210	**Hover / tint discipline:** `--accent-hover` ≈ 5% darker on the same hue; `--accent-tint` ≈ 8–10% alpha of accent; `--on-accent` must clear APCA Lc ≥ 60 against the filled button.
211	
212	**Dark mode:** lift accent lightness ~15–20% on dark surfaces (see each preset's dark mapping). Re-verify contrast after swap.
213	
214	**Marketing vs product:** landings and portfolios may rotate accent **and** theme preset; dashboards and auth rotate accent only unless the user asks for a full re-skin.
215	
216	## Premium palette families (artisan / luxury / wellness briefs)
217	
218	"Premium" briefs converge on one palette — warm cream background, brass/clay accent, espresso text — until every generated artisan site is interchangeable. Unless the brief names those colors, rotate through distinct families (one per build, never the same family twice in a row):
219	
220	| Family | Recipe | Reads as |
221	|---|---|---|
222	| **Cold luxury** | silver-grey neutrals + chrome + smoke dark | precision, engineering premium |
223	| **Forest** | deep green + bone + amber accent | outdoor heritage, built-to-last |
224	| **Black & tan** | true off-black + warm tan, hard contrast, no beige | leather-goods, deliberate |
225	| **Cobalt + cream** | one saturated blue against a single neutral | confident, modern craft |
226	| **Terracotta + slate** | warm rust against cool grey | earthy without the beige wash |
227	| **Mono + pop** | off-white + off-black + one bright accent | gallery, editorial-modern |
228	
229	Warmth can come from typography, imagery, and copy — it doesn't have to live in the background color. Verify AA contrast after picking; dark-mode mapping per the preset rules above.
230

